{"title":"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/f/56f678142f857f6e2ac92fe29045106a5c42d7c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$82~460$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/4/474bed20b2963f8f2e20e9e523ff94cef3522fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 0 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 5 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 4 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 7 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"388\" height=\"18\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can do long division to find the answer. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/f/14f158176636f8b0c44865dcbbdaa5571c048d7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\times 10~000 = 80~000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"159\" height=\"15\" />, so there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/2/aa26c0bf95cb1ff8c550a983db596ab7a9ba21b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2460$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> remaining.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> does not go into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we have to bring the next digit.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> goes into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times with no remainder, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is remaining.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> goes into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times, but there is a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a280a5608b9a4167a62fab57a71951aca4f37a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60 - 8 \\times 7 = 60 - 56 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"245\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1.5_.28shorter_method.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5_(shorter_method)\">Solution 1.5 (shorter method)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5 (shorter method)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/139cb9699073a95c16221e8de9573bf82beabd02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000 = 2^3 \\times 5^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" /> divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/0/5b0dd9a4f25aeb554dbec20cc120d4b1f06106d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 = 2^3$\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> gives a whole number, only the last three digits matter.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/e/63e4a6382961b152fffb6f72ff7db4f4df7ebd9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400 = 8 \\times 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> remaining. We can then see the remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e657cbbdfa9cc24ea60f6a255d3a116816e0ae5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a18b645049f40d9cec7bc1fa05cc5c25bf7f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60 = 8 \\times 7 + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEM